-lg px-4 py-3 text-center font-medium text-gray-800 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:scale-[1.02] transition-all\">Sweetie</div><div class=\"bg-white/80 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center font-medium text-gray-800 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:scale-[1.02] transition-all\">Tiny Tot</div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"ad-slot my-8 mx-auto max-w-[728px] \" data-ad-position=\"content\"><div class=\"border-2 border-dashed border-gray-300 rounded-lg bg-gray-50 flex items-center justify-center h-[90px] text-gray-400 text-sm select-none\">Ad - After Name Lists (300×250)</div></div></section><section class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-8\">❓ Frequently Asked Questions About <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> Names</h2><div class=\"space-y-3\"><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">What makes a good african civet name?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">A good african civet name should match your pet&#x27;s personality, be easy to pronounce and remember, and ideally be one or two syllables. The best names reflect something unique about the animal while being practical for everyday use.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Should I choose a name based on my african civet&#x27;s appearance?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Absolutely! african civet&#x27;s distinctive features make wonderful naming inspiration. Names based on color, size, or markings create an immediate connection and help others appreciate your pet&#x27;s unique beauty.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Can I use a human name for my african civet?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Human names are very popular for pets! Names like Charlie, Max, Luna, and Bella work wonderfully and can make your bond with your african civet feel even more personal and meaningful.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">How many names should I consider before choosing?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">We recommend shortlisting 3-5 favorite names, then testing them over a few days. Say each name aloud during different activities — the one that consistently feels natural is your winner.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Do african civets respond better to certain sounds?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Animals tend to respond best to names ending in a vowel sound, especially &#x27;ee&#x27; sounds like Charlie or Lucy. Names with hard consonants at the beginning (like K, T, B) also capture attention more effectively.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">What makes a good name for a African Civet?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">A good African Civet name is clear, easy to pronounce, and fits your pet&#x27;s personality. Avoid names that sound like commands or household names. The best names often come from observing your African Civet&#x27;s habits and character — the right name will feel natural after a few days of use.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Can I give my African Civet a humorous or unusual name?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Absolutely — humorous and unusual names often become beloved conversation starters. The key is ensuring the name brings you joy rather than embarrassment when called in public. If you smile every time you say it, it&#x27;s the right name regardless of convention.</p></details></div></section><section class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-8\">📖 <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> Naming Guide</h2><div class=\"bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm border border-gray-100\"><ul class=\"space-y-3\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->1</span><span>Spend time observing your african civet&#x27;s behavior before finalizing a name — the right name often reveals itself through personality.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->2</span><span>Choose a name that is easy to pronounce and won&#x27;t embarrass you when calling it in public.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->3</span><span>Consider names with two syllables — they are short enough for quick recognition but distinct enough to avoid confusion.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->4</span><span>Test your chosen name for a full week before committing. The name that survives daily use is the right one.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->5</span><span>Avoid names that sound similar to common commands like &#x27;no&#x27;, &#x27;stay&#x27;, or &#x27;come&#x27;.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->6</span><span>Involve your family in the naming process — the name should feel right to everyone who will interact with your african civet.</span></li></ul></div></section><section class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 space-y-10\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8\"><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-6\">🔗 <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> Name Categories</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\"><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/african-civet-names/\">📛<!-- --> <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> <!-- -->Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/male-african-civet-names/\">♂️<!-- --> <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> <!-- -->Male Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/female-african-civet-names/\">♀️<!-- --> <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> <!-- -->Female Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/cute-african-civet-names/\">💕<!-- --> <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> <!-- -->Cute Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/funny-african-civet-names/\">😂<!-- --> <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> <!-- -->Funny Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/fantasy-african-civet-names/\">🧙<!-- --> <!-- -->African Civet<!-- --> <!-- -->Fantasy Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition